=== Rigid body ===

If a [[mechanical system]] is constrained to move parallel to a fixed plane, then the rotation of a body in the system occurs around an axis __MATH_115__ parallel to this plane. In this case, the moment of inertia of the mass in this system is a scalar known as the ''polar moment of inertia''. The definition of the polar moment of inertia can be obtained by considering momentum, kinetic energy and Newton's laws for the planar movement of a rigid system of particles.

